In src/sema/types.rs, the Type enum has separate Var, IntVar, FloatVar variants which complicates pattern matching. Many functions need 13+ match arms.

Current:
```rust
pub enum Type {
    Primitive, Var, IntVar, FloatVar, Ref, Array, Slice,
    Tuple, Struct, FnPtr, String, Error, Alias, Param, SelfType
}
```

Proposed:
```rust
pub enum InferVar { Generic(u32), Integer(u32), Float(u32) }
pub enum Type {
    Infer(InferVar),  // Consolidates Var, IntVar, FloatVar
    // ...remaining variants
}
```

No compile() function showing typical usage. Users must manually chain:
```rust
let parse = parse(source);
let ctx = SemanticContext::new();
let resolve_result = Resolver::new(&mut ctx).resolve(&ast);
let infer_result = infer(&source_file, resolve_result);
```
Proposed: Add convenience API and examples in lib.rs.

In src/parser/expr/mod.rs (lines 146-205), operator precedence uses magic numbers:
```rust
Token::Eq | Token::PlusEq | ... => Some((2, 1)),  // What does 2,1 mean?
Token::PipePipe => Some((3, 4)),  // Why these values?
```

Proposed Fix: Define named constants:
```rust
const BP_ASSIGNMENT: (u8, u8) = (2, 1);
const BP_LOGICAL_OR: (u8, u8) = (3, 4);
const BP_LOGICAL_AND: (u8, u8) = (5, 6);
// etc.
```
